data: {"id":"chatcmpl-e820d851-9653-452b-8be4-61f63c9cf9aa","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795553188,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"The write-sequence AVL tree efficiently detects range conflicts using `hasWriteInRange`. Every key `K` within subtree `n` satisfies `subLo < K < subHi`, where `subLo` and `subHi` are the lower and upper bounds of n's keys. If `lo <= subLo` AND `subHi <= hi`, every key `K` in subtree `n` falls within the query range `[lo, hi]`.  Given `n.maxSeq > minSeq`, at least one node's key is within the range `lo <= K <= hi`, triggering a conflict. The logic correctly returns true.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl-e820d851-9653-452b-8be4-61f63c9cf9aa","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795553188,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"The `hasWriteInRange` function's logic is traced meticulously, checking `n.maxSeq <= minSeq` to enable pruning. Subtree range checks (`lo <= subLo && subHi <= hi`) allow early `true` returns. The primary case is the direct key comparison (`lo <= n.key <= hi && n.lastSeq > minSeq`), followed by recursive calls to `n.left` and `n.right` subtrees. The code handles range intersections and efficiently prunes the search space by returning early when possible.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl-e820d851-9653-452b-8be4-61f63c9cf9aa","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795553188,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"The write-sequence tree's range conflict check, `hasWriteInRange`, is examined. The logic is now understood: the method correctly navigates and prunes the AVL tree. The conditions for recursive calls, and for returning early, are verified for correctness. The function is verified: if `lo <= n.key <= hi` and if there exists a key where `lastWriteSeq` is greater than `minSeq`, it will return `true` at the node, otherwise, the method will keep searching. The boundary cases `lo == hi` and empty ranges are verified and confirmed to be correct.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl-e820d851-9653-452b-8be4-61f63c9cf9aa","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795553188,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"The write-sequence AVL tree efficiently detects range conflicts. Examining edge cases and test scenarios confirms the logic's correctness, including situations with a single key and more complex subtrees. The code now optimizes range conflict checks by pruning the search space based on `maxSeq`. Further testing with overlapping range queries validates performance.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

