data: {"id":"chatcmpl-e820d851-9653-452b-8be4-61f63c9cf9aa","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795553188,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"The record validation order is crucial: R6 (torn tail) *precedes* R7 (invalid type).  If a record is cut short (L - p <= 2), it's a torn tail, *not* an invalid type.  Rules are validated in sequence: R5, R6, R7, R8, R9, and R10.  If a truncated record passes R6 (torn tail), subsequent rules like R7 (invalid type) are then evaluated. Section 7.2 dictates that R7 applies to every record with at least 3 bytes remaining, including malformed records that fail subsequent checks. The examples of validation of various scenarios are now validated.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

